course: dictionary
lesson: 3769
title: Folk: people, music and tales
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Folk most often means people, especially ordinary people: «Some folk are like that, pet.» Here folk simply means people in general. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Folk also appears in phrases. A folk tale is a story passed down by word of mouth, often with no known author, such as Jack and the Beanstalk. A folk song or folk dance belongs to ordinary people and has been handed down from one generation to the next. The word folk in the phrase is your clue.
explain: Informal talk changes the meaning again. Your «folks» are your parents or family, as in «my folks». «Hi, folks!» is a friendly way to speak to a group. Ask yourself: is this about a group of people, a family, or a style of music?
fact: Folk means people, especially ordinary people.
fact: «Folks» in informal speech can mean your parents or family.
fact: A folk tale or folk song is passed down by word of mouth, often with no known author.
fact: Folk music and folk dance are traditional music and dance of a place, passed down by ordinary people.
fact: «Hi, folks!» is a friendly way to speak to a group of people.
exercise: «Some folk are like that, pet.» What does folk mean in this sentence? | A type of dance | *People in general | A fairy tale about a wolf | A family dog
exercise: The teacher says, «We are learning a folk song from the old days.» What is a folk song? | A song sung only in a school hall | A song that is played on a phone | A song written by a famous singer last year | *A traditional song passed down by ordinary people
exercise: «Hi, folks, let's get started.» What does folks mean here? | Your parents or family | Ordinary people from the country | A traditional dance | *A friendly way to speak to a group of people
test: Ella says, «My folks are coming to watch the show.» Who are her folks? | A folk tale she has read | Her favourite singers | *Her parents or family | A group of ordinary people
test: The class learns a folk dance from Scotland. What is a folk dance? | A dance done in space | A dance only the teacher knows | *A traditional dance of a place, passed down by ordinary people | A dance invented in a film last year
exam: In «a folk tale», what does folk mean? | A friendly greeting to a group | Your parents or family | *A story passed down by ordinary people, with no known author | A story written by one famous author
